								<div class="title" id="post-title-3725760">
																		there&#039;s one thing that really bothers me about this
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ratsy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3050018); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3050018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609559527" alt="ratsy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3050018)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ratsy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3050018); return false;" >ratsy</a></span> <span class="odate time_1519927542 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Mar 2018 18:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3725760">
									

<p>And that's the tenses. You have a lot of phrases like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He <strong>says</strong> as his scowl <strong>intensified</strong>.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Says is present tense. Intensified is past tense. This is just bad writing, like if I said, &quot;I am going to the store and then I bought apples there.&quot; Stick to one &#8212; either, &quot;he says as his scowl intensifies,&quot; or &quot;he said as his scowl intensified.&quot;</p>
<p>There's a lot of phrases like this. It completely quelled any enjoyment I could have gotten from this.</p>
<p>Otherwise I'd probably novote. I didn't find it particularly entertaining, but other that this issue getting on my nerves, I don't dislike it.</p>

							</div>

								
					
